wcristalle@hotmail.com (Artemis the Ranger) writes:

> On a related topic, it's always struck me as sort of weird that the
> more intelligent pets never decide to rebel against their owners. I
> mean, in real life, I can't even get my *dog* to do what I want. Why
> should your pet obey you if it is a Archon and you have just been
> polymorphed into a violet fungus? :-)

Well, you can't actually _command_ your pet in Nethack (unless someone
has written a patch to allow this).  All you can do to control it is
bribe it with treats, move it around with a leash or magic whistle,
and ride it if it's the right type of monster.  Perhaps intelligent
pets should object to being leashed (or ridden?), though.  It is also
strange that a pet Elvenking can be trained with tripe rations; lembas
should be better, and money or equipment even better.

> On a more serious bent, though, shouldn't intelligence figure into the
> tameness of a pet? The more intelligent a pet is, it seems to me, the
> less likely that it will stay tame. On the other hand, the more
> intelligent a pet is, the easier it should be for it to learn tricks
> like fetching objects from stores.

Maybe intelligent pets have their own reasons for travelling with
you.  They might prefer the thrill of the adventuring life, or a share
of the glory you'll get when you offer the Amulet, to their safe but
pointless life in the dungeons.

We could think about the various ways that pets become tame, and how
likely it is that a pet tamed in each of these ways will go wild.  For
example, a cat or dog follows you just because you once fed it tripe -
if you then polymorph it into something intelligent, it shouldn't have
any trouble realising that that isn't a very good reason to keep
serving you.  Breaking free from the mind-controlling magic of charm
monster would be harder, but perhaps not impossible since abandoned
pets will eventually go wild.

Should any intelligent pets have an ethical code?  It's a bit strange
that when a monster is tamed, it becomes indiscriminately violent
towards everyone but you, even peacefuls.  Lawful intelligent pets
might refuse to steal from shops, while chaotics would be very happy
to grab everything and walk out.
Eva.

